# StayFinder final API requests
# Run one request at a time against a development database with migrations through 025.
# Expected results are assertions; observed live results are in docs/criteria-evidence.md.
# Use disposable fixtures and separate cookie stores. Never commit credentials.
# Set IDs from responses; keep actor cookies in private tooling or an ignored copy.
# Run logout LAST. Cancellation/deletion change fixtures: follow each precondition.
# For full boundary/concurrency/direct-database coverage, run the linked live runners
# in requests/README.md. All seven VG rules have executable runners.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@frontendOrigin = http://localhost:3001
@propertyId = REPLACE_WITH_EXISTING_PROPERTY_UUID
@bookingId = REPLACE_WITH_TEST_BOOKING_UUID
@otherBookingId = REPLACE_WITH_OTHER_GUEST_BOOKING_UUID
@missingId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@ownerCookies = REPLACE_LOCALLY_WITH_OWNER_COOKIE_HEADER
@guestCookies = REPLACE_LOCALLY_WITH_GUEST_A_COOKIE_HEADER
@otherGuestCookies = REPLACE_LOCALLY_WITH_GUEST_B_COOKIE_HEADER
@checkIn = 2030-06-10
@checkOut = 2030-06-13
# dates must be future dates when running; configure the overlap fixture below.

### API status - expected 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### property list - expected 200, array
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties

### property details - expected 200, object (replace propertyId)
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties/{{propertyId}}

### missing property - expected 404 (ensure missingId is absent)
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties/{{missingId}}

### missing route - expected 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/route-that-does-not-exist

### invalid booking body - expected 400 with validation errors
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Cookie: {{guestCookies}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "property_id": "{{propertyId}}",
  "guest_name": "Test Guest",
  "guest_email": "not-an-email",
  "check_in": "{{checkIn}}",
  "check_out": "{{checkOut}}",
  "guests": 0
}

### G1 registration - expected 201, possibly confirmation required
# Supply email/password through local request tooling; these are placeholders.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "REPLACE_LOCALLY_WITH_TEST_EMAIL",
  "password": "REPLACE_LOCALLY_WITH_TEST_PASSWORD"
}

### G1 login - expected 200 and session Set-Cookie headers
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "REPLACE_LOCALLY_WITH_TEST_EMAIL",
  "password": "REPLACE_LOCALLY_WITH_TEST_PASSWORD"
}

### G2 current user - expected 200 and guest A identity
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Cookie: {{guestCookies}}

### G2 anonymous current user - expected 401
# Ensure the request tool is not automatically attaching cookies.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### G6 anonymous create - expected 401, no inserted row
# Must use a clean client/cookie jar with no automatically attached session.
POST {{baseUrl}}/properties
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Disposable test property",
  "description": "Property reserved for API verification",
  "location": "Test City",
  "price_per_night": 1000,
  "max_guests": 2
}

### G6/VG1 owner create - expected 201 and derived owner identity
# Save returned property_id locally; use that ID as propertyId for later tests.
POST {{baseUrl}}/properties
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Cookie: {{ownerCookies}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Disposable test property",
  "description": "Property reserved for API verification",
  "location": "Test City",
  "price_per_night": 1000,
  "max_guests": 2
}

### VG1 nonowner property update - denied, property unchanged
# Expected 404: API filters by owner_id; verify the property is unchanged.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/properties/{{propertyId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Cookie: {{guestCookies}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Unauthorized change" }

### G5/G8 filtering and descending sort - expected 200
# Verify every returned value satisfies the filters.
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties?location=Test%20City&max_price=1000&guests=2&sort=desc

### G8 ascending sort - expected 200, monotonic prices
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties?sort=asc

### G9/VG3/VG6 booking at capacity - expected 201
# For the test property above: 3 nights * 1000 = 3000, status pending.
# Ensure these dates are free before sending; save returned booking_id locally.
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Cookie: {{guestCookies}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "property_id": "{{propertyId}}",
  "guest_name": "Test Guest A",
  "guest_email": "guest-a@example.com",
  "check_in": "{{checkIn}}",
  "check_out": "{{checkOut}}",
  "guests": 2
}

### VG1 guest B reads guest A booking - expected 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Cookie: {{otherGuestCookies}}

### VG1 guest A sees only permitted bookings - expected 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Cookie: {{guestCookies}}

### VG1 owner sees bookings for their property - expected 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings?property_id={{propertyId}}
Cookie: {{ownerCookies}}

### VG2 overlapping creation - expected 409 with clear conflict
# Fixture: guest A's pending/confirmed booking already occupies checkIn/checkOut.
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Cookie: {{otherGuestCookies}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "property_id": "{{propertyId}}",
  "guest_name": "Test Guest B",
  "guest_email": "guest-b@example.com",
  "check_in": "{{checkIn}}",
  "check_out": "{{checkOut}}",
  "guests": 1
}

### VG2 unchanged dates do not conflict with the same booking
# Run before confirmation/cancellation; expected 200, unchanged ID.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Cookie: {{guestCookies}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "property_id": "{{propertyId}}",
  "guest_name": "Test Guest A",
  "guest_email": "guest-a@example.com",
  "check_in": "{{checkIn}}",
  "check_out": "{{checkOut}}",
  "guests": 2,
  "status": "pending"
}

